# --- the account file - never commit ---------------------------------------
# docs/gcontactssync.txt.sample is the template and IS tracked.
gcontactssync.txt

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Qt for Symbian supports in-source builds only, so a lot of generated files land next to the
# sources. Everything below is produced by qmake, sbs or createpackage.
build/
build-cli/
build-desktop/
*.o
*.obj
moc_*.cpp
qrc_*.cpp
ui_*.h
Makefile*
tmp/
release/
debug/
.make.cache
build.log

# Generated by qmake from GContactsSync.pro - never edited by hand. Wildcards rather than exact
# names: qmake emits more of these than is obvious (GContactsSync_exe.mmp, for one).
*.pkg
*.rss
# ...except this one, which is hand-written source: the startup list entry. The wildcard is
# aimed at GContactsSync.rss and GContactsSync_reg.rss, which qmake generates.
!GContactsSync_startup.rss
*.loc
*.mmp
*.mif
bld.inf
# dumpsis -x unpacks a package into a directory named after it.
GContactsSync_*/

# The packages. Kept on disk - build-symbian.cmd never deletes an older one, and a previous .sis
# is the quickest way back to a working build - but not committed: they are build output, and one
# per version adds up fast.
*.sis
*.sisx
